<BaseLayout
  title="About ｜ PubMed Trivia"
  description="PubMed Trivia turns peer-reviewed research from PubMed into bite-sized daily trivia for general readers."
  lang="en"
>
  <article>
    <h1>About</h1>

    <h2>Mission</h2>
    <p>
      PubMed Trivia turns peer-reviewed research from
      <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">PubMed</a> — the U.S. National Library of Medicine's database — into
      short, accurate trivia for curious general readers. We focus on review articles and meta-analyses
      in psychology and biology.
    </p>

    <h2>Topics we cover</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Psychology, sleep, memory, learning, and decision-making</li>
      <li>Animal behavior, evolutionary biology, ecology, anthropology</li>
      <li>Lifestyle and health associations (not medical advice)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Editorial standards</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We use <strong>review articles and meta-analyses</strong> rather than single case reports or retracted studies.</li>
      <li>We never confuse <strong>association with causation</strong>. We translate carefully.</li>
      <li>Japanese and English versions are written independently from the source abstract, not via double-translation.</li>
      <li>Drafting is assisted by Anthropic's Claude API.</li>
      <li>Every article links to the original paper via PMID.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      Content on this site is general-interest trivia, not medical advice. For health-related decisions,
      please consult a licensed professional. If you find inaccuracies, please reach out.
    </p>

    <h2>Ads and affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      This site participates in third-party advertising and the Amazon Associates Program. See our
      <a href="/en/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for details.
    </p>

